      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{69d28b55a4b6d376ad9cf70b|full_name} Notifications/requests =/= join permissions. I believe you can reproduce this with a friend:\n\n1. Agree on a specific world to check mutually with a friend.\n\n2. Go on orange/red status.\n\n3. Create a Friends+ instance in that world and join it.\n\n4. Wait a few minutes.\n\n5. Communicate to your friend to check available instances from the world page in-app, without sending an invite. They should be able to see your Friends+ instance (on the right hand side), and can join you.\n\nThe API makes it easier to join people on orange/red with some external tooling (not condoning this to be compliant use of the API).\n\nIf you don't want to be joinable, be in Secure Instances (Invite/Invite+) or close the instance if you have permissions to do so.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
